  "a73": {
   "titolo": "Dive into new topics with immersive explorations in the Gemini app.",
   "link": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/immersive-explorations-student-hub/",
   "data": "2026-10-28T18:00:00+00:00",
   "testo": "Dive into new topics with immersive explorations in the Gemini app. The Gemini app now has a library of immersive explorations, giving you an interactive, visual way to explore topics layer-by-layer, from microscopic systems to deep space and more. You can access this library in the Gemini student hub by clicking on “Try immersive explorations” and will soon be able to access these immersive explorations directly in a chat conversation with Gemini. Whether it’s tracing trade routes on the Silk Road, peering inside a jet engine, or studying the physics of lightning, each scene unfolds into interactive and guided experiences. Tap a label to dig deeper, journeying from sweeping planetary scales straight down to molecules and atoms. Immersive explorations will soon include audio narration to walk you through each layer. This feature is available to all users in English, Indonesian, Hindi, Brazilian Portuguese, French, and simplified Chinese. Users in all other languages currently receive an English-only experience, with more languages coming soon. Explore the feature today.",
   "fonte": "Google (blog ufficiale)",
   "tipo": "ufficiale",
   "solo_titolo": false,
   "categoria": "Laboratori",
   "id": "a73",
   "testo_completo": true
  },
  "a77": {
   "titolo": "Build and manage Connected Apps in one place",
   "link": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/connected-apps-one-place/",
   "data": "2026-10-28T17:00:00+00:00",
   "testo": "Build and manage Connected Apps in one place From ordering groceries to making playlists, Connected Apps in Search and the Gemini app have made everyday tasks faster and easier. To help users get more done, today we’re launching the preview of our Connected Apps Platform, a unified way for more app developers to bring their capabilities directly into Gemini and Search. We’re also rolling out a new set of Connected Apps partners to give people even more ways to streamline their day. Manage Connected Apps with ease The Connected Apps Platform gives developers the opportunity to build once and reach high-intent users across both Search and the Gemini app. Developers integrate with a cloud-hosted MCP server or Android MCP using the AppFunctions APIs, then use the Google Connected Console to register, test, and submit their app. Before review, developers choose whether it will go live in Search, the Gemini app, or both. Once live, you can track traffic, latency, and error rates, and keep control of your brand identity, including verified logos and authenticated accounts. We're opening access in phases, and will add more developers, markets, and Google products over the coming months. Sign up for the preview and explore the documentation at developers.google.com/connected-apps. Connect to your favorite tools We’ve launched more than 50 Connected Apps between Search and Gemini in areas ranging from productivity and event ticketing to health and fitness. Integrations with partners like Adobe, Experian, Localiza, and Peloton are live for users in Gemini, and in the coming weeks, we’ll be bringing these Connected Apps to Search as well. Among other apps, we'll also be launching a new integration with Calm across both Search and Gemini. To see all the Connected Apps you can acces…",
   "fonte": "Google Gemini (blog)",
   "tipo": "ufficiale",
   "solo_titolo": false,
   "categoria": "Laboratori",
   "id": "a77",
   "testo_completo": true
  },
